  <page_number>35</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>C. ij.</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Non ante seclis visa prioribus,</l>
    <l n="2">Et Marte quouis horridior fames</l>
    <l n="3">Grassata jamdudum, luesque</l>
    <l n="4">Innumeras vacuavit urbes.</l>
    <l n="5">Præsentis ævi dicere quæ Lyra,</l>
    <l n="6">Quæ lingua possit funera tristia?</l>
    <l n="7">Nam quisque mensis, nam lapillo est</l>
    <l n="8">Quæque dies memoranda nigro.</l>
    <l n="9">Videre tristes Bullonium ducem</l>
    <l n="10">Jam Calendæ frigore pallidum,</l>
    <l n="11">Lethæo &amp; extinctum dolore</l>
    <l n="12">Perpetuo juvenem requirent.</l>
    <l n="13">Illum juventæ, &amp; patrius vigor,</l>
    <l n="14">Et vera virtus impulerat pio</l>
    <l n="15">Cum fratre, non suetos labores</l>
    <l n="16">Pro patria, &amp; pietate ferre.</l>
    <l n="17">Sed supplicanti nescia mors manu</l>
    <l n="18">Votisve flecti membra doloribus</l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Defessa longis utriusque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Cruda rapit properante fato. Vix</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>vix Calendis finierat dies</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Sacrata Ioui, nuntius attulit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Heroa Cleruanum fidelem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Lethifero periisse morbo:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Cuius modestis pectoribus fides</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Antiqua sedit, rebus &amp; asperis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Spectata semper, clariorque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Ambiguis nituit periclis.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Doubtful readings: "flecti" (ct ligature), "Quæ" in line 6 (initial letter partly underlined in the scan), "Quæque" in line 8. Ligatures æ and ct are rendered as printed. The first line is a fragment of the poem's opening line, cut off at the left; the poem continues from the previous page. Printed "vtriusque" and "vix" are normalised as u/v rules require.</notes>
</page>
